NAME
    watch - track reads/writes to a memory range

SYNOPSIS
    watch add <space> <addr> <len> [write|read|both]
    watch list
    watch log <id> [<count>]
    watch summary <id>
    watch clear <id>
    watch remove <id>

DESCRIPTION
    'add' registers a watch over <addr>..<addr>+<len>-1 in <space> (default
    kind: write) and starts recording matching accesses as they happen -
    this is a LIVE, triggered mechanism (see 'framelog' for the sampled-
    every-frame alternative, and 'callers'/'writers'/'readers' for static
    analysis that doesn't require the access to actually happen first).
    'log' shows a watch's recorded (sequence, kind, address, value, context)
    events, newest last. 'summary' groups those events by access site
    instead of listing every one - the dynamic, addressing-mode-agnostic
    equivalent of 'readers'/'writers'. 'clear' empties a watch's recorded
    events without removing the watch itself; 'remove' deletes it entirely.

EXAMPLES
    watch add WRAM 13c6 1
    watch log 1
    watch summary 1
